IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`

-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 25 September 2024.
-- LAYER 1, PART 10A, Division 4 (ADMINISTRATIVE AND GENERAL PROVISIONS, ss 45P to 45T). Section 45T carries the Part's meanings, among them "social media service" and "Singapore end-user link".
-- These rules state the 2024 consolidation (Part 10A entered wef 1 February 2023).

§ `45P. Regulations`

-- src:3432 | 45P.—(1) The Authority may, with the approval of the Minister,
-- src:3433 | make regulations which are required or permitted to be prescribed by
-- src:3434 | this Part or are necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying
-- src:3435 | out or giving effect to this Part.
@ref s 45P(1) (src:3432-3435)
GIVEN `the Authority made the regulations with the approval of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45P(1) the regulations are validly made` MEANS `the Authority made the regulations with the approval of the Minister`

-- src:3437 | (2) All subsidiary legislation made under this Part must be
-- src:3438 | presented to Parliament as soon as possible after publication in the
-- src:3439 | Gazette.
@ref s 45P(2) (src:3437-3439)
GIVEN `the subsidiary legislation was presented to Parliament as soon as possible after publication in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45P(2) the subsidiary legislation has been presented to Parliament as the subsection requires` MEANS `the subsidiary legislation was presented to Parliament as soon as possible after publication in the Gazette`

§ `45Q. Incorporation by reference`

-- src:3445 | 45Q.—(1) Any subsidiary legislation made under this Part or any
-- src:3446 | online Code of Practice may make provision for or in relation to a
-- src:3447 | matter by applying, adopting or incorporating by reference, with or
-- src:3448 | without modification, any material contained in any standard, rule,
-- src:3449 | requirement, specification or other document, as in force at a
-- src:3450 | particular time or from time to time, which relates to any matter with
-- src:3451 | which the subsidiary legislation or online Code of Practice deals,
-- src:3452 | even if the standard, rule, requirement, specification or other
-- src:3453 | document does not yet exist when the subsidiary legislation or
-- src:3454 | online Code of Practice is made.
@ref s 45Q(1) (src:3445-3454)
GIVEN `the material relates to a matter with which the subsidiary legislation or online Code of Practice deals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45Q(1) the subsidiary legislation or Code may incorporate the material by reference, as in force at a particular time or from time to time, even if it does not yet exist` MEANS
    `the material relates to a matter with which the subsidiary legislation or online Code of Practice deals`

-- src:3459 | (2) Any material referred to in subsection (1) may be applied,
-- src:3460 | adopted or incorporated by reference in any subsidiary legislation
-- src:3461 | made under this Part or any online Code of Practice —
-- src:3463 | (a) in whole or in part; or
-- src:3465 | (b) with modifications, additions, or variations specified in the
-- src:3466 | subsidiary legislation or online Code of Practice, as the
-- src:3467 | case may be.
@ref s 45Q(2) (src:3459-3467)
GIVEN `the material is incorporated in whole or in part, or with modifications, additions or variations specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45Q(2) the material may be incorporated in that way` MEANS `the material is incorporated in whole or in part, or with modifications, additions or variations specified`

-- src:3469 | (3) A copy of any material applied, adopted or incorporated by
-- src:3470 | reference in any subsidiary legislation made under this Part or any
-- src:3471 | online Code of Practice, including any amendment to, or replacement
-- src:3472 | of, the material, must be —
-- src:3474 | (a) certified as a correct copy of the material by the Minister or
-- src:3475 | the Authority, as the case may be; and
-- src:3477 | (b) retained by the Authority.
@ref s 45Q(3) (src:3469-3477)
GIVEN `a copy of the material, including any amendment or replacement, was certified as a correct copy by the Minister or the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority retained the copy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45Q(3) the copy has been certified and retained as the subsection requires` MEANS
    `a copy of the material, including any amendment or replacement, was certified as a correct copy by the Minister or the Authority` AND `the Authority retained the copy`

-- src:3479 | (4) Any material applied, adopted or incorporated in any subsidiary
-- src:3480 | legislation made under this Part or any online Code of Practice by
-- src:3481 | reference under subsection (1) is to be treated for all purposes as
-- src:3482 | forming part of the subsidiary legislation or online Code of Practice;
-- src:3483 | and, unless otherwise provided in the subsidiary legislation or online
-- src:3484 | Code of Practice, every amendment to any material incorporated by
-- src:3485 | reference under subsection (1) that is made by the person or
-- src:3486 | organisation originating the material is, subject to subsections (5)
-- src:3487 | and (6), to be treated as being a part of that subsidiary legislation or
-- src:3488 | online Code of Practice, as the case may be.
@ref s 45Q(4) (src:3479-3488)
GIVEN `the material is incorporated by reference under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45Q(4) the material is treated for all purposes as forming part of the subsidiary legislation or Code` MEANS
    IF `the material is incorporated by reference under subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3490 | (5) Where any material referred to in subsection (1) is applied,
-- src:3491 | adopted or incorporated by reference in any subsidiary legislation
-- src:3492 | made under this Part or any online Code of Practice, the Authority
-- src:3493 | must give notice in the Gazette stating —
-- src:3495 | (a) that the material is incorporated in the subsidiary
-- src:3496 | legislation made under this Part or online Code of
-- src:3497 | Practice and the date on which the relevant provision in
-- src:3498 | the subsidiary legislation or online Code of Practice was
-- src:3499 | made;
-- src:3504 | (b) that the material is available for inspection during working
-- src:3505 | hours, free of charge;
-- src:3507 | (c) the place where the material can be inspected without
-- src:3508 | charge;
-- src:3510 | (d) that copies of the material can be purchased;
-- src:3512 | (e) the place where copies of the material can be purchased;
-- src:3513 | and
-- src:3515 | (f) if copies of the material are available in other ways, the
-- src:3516 | details of where or how the material can be accessed or
-- src:3517 | obtained.
@ref s 45Q(5) (src:3490-3517)
GIVEN `the Authority gave notice in the Gazette stating the incorporation and the date of the provision, that the material may be inspected free of charge during working hours and where, that copies can be purchased and where, and any other ways the material can be accessed or obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45Q(5) the Authority has given the notice the subsection requires` MEANS
    `the Authority gave notice in the Gazette stating the incorporation and the date of the provision, that the material may be inspected free of charge during working hours and where, that copies can be purchased and where, and any other ways the material can be accessed or obtained`

-- src:3519 | (6) In this section, “modification” includes omissions, additions
-- src:3520 | and substitutions.
@ref s 45Q(6) (src:3519-3520)
GIVEN `it is an omission, addition or substitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45Q(6) modification includes this` MEANS
    IF `it is an omission, addition or substitution` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `45R. Interface with other laws and civil liability`

-- src:3526 | 45R.—(1) To avoid doubt, section 26(1) of the Electronic
-- src:3527 | Transactions Act 2010 (which relates to the limitation of liability
-- src:3528 | against network service providers) applies in relation to any liability
-- src:3529 | under this Part other than liability under section 45E, 45F or 45N.
@ref s 45R(1) (src:3526-3529)
GIVEN `the liability is under section 45E, 45F or 45N` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45R(1) section 26(1) of the Electronic Transactions Act 2010 applies in relation to the liability` MEANS
    NOT `the liability is under section 45E, 45F or 45N`

-- src:3531 | (2) Nothing in section 45J or 45M is to be construed —
-- src:3533 | (a) as conferring a right of action in any civil proceedings in
-- src:3534 | respect of any contravention of any provision of this Part or
-- src:3535 | an online Code of Practice; or
-- src:3537 | (b) as conferring a defence to an action in any civil
-- src:3538 | proceedings or as otherwise affecting a right of action in
-- src:3539 | any civil proceedings.
@ref s 45R(2) (src:3531-3539)
GIVEN `it is a right of action in civil proceedings for a contravention of a provision of this Part or an online Code of Practice, or a defence to or other effect on a right of action in civil proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45R(2) section 45J or 45M is to be construed as conferring it` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:3541 | (3) For the purposes of sections 45E(1), 45F(1), 45H and 45I, a
-- src:3542 | person is to be disregarded as a Singapore end-user using an online
-- src:3543 | communication service if the person accesses content in any of the
-- src:3544 | following circumstances:
-- src:3546 | (a) the accessing of the content is necessary for enforcing this
-- src:3547 | Act or any other written law;
-- src:3552 | (b) the accessing of the content is necessary for monitoring
-- src:3553 | compliance with, or investigating a contravention of, this
-- src:3554 | Act or any other written law;
-- src:3556 | (c) the accessing of the content is solely for the purposes of
-- src:3557 | proceedings in a Singapore court or tribunal;
-- src:3559 | (d) the accessing of the content is both —
-- src:3561 | (i) necessary and solely for, or of assistance in,
-- src:3562 | conducting scientific, medical, academic or
-- src:3563 | historical research; and
-- src:3565 | (ii) reasonable in the circumstances for the purpose of
-- src:3566 | conducting that scientific, medical, academic or
-- src:3567 | historical research.
@ref s 45R(3) (src:3541-3567)
GIVEN `the person accesses the content as necessary for enforcing this Act or another written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person accesses the content as necessary for monitoring compliance with, or investigating a contravention of, this Act or another written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person accesses the content solely for the purposes of proceedings in a Singapore court or tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person accesses the content as necessary and solely for, or of assistance in, scientific, medical, academic or historical research, and it is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45R(3) the person is disregarded as a Singapore end-user using the online communication service` MEANS
    `the person accesses the content as necessary for enforcing this Act or another written law` OR `the person accesses the content as necessary for monitoring compliance with, or investigating a contravention of, this Act or another written law` OR `the person accesses the content solely for the purposes of proceedings in a Singapore court or tribunal` OR `the person accesses the content as necessary and solely for, or of assistance in, scientific, medical, academic or historical research, and it is reasonable in the circumstances`

§ `45S. Modification of section 50`

-- src:3573 | 45S.—(1) Where the person that commits an offence under
-- src:3574 | section 50(2) or (3) is a provider of a regulated online
-- src:3575 | communication service and with respect to documents or
-- src:3576 | information relating to that service, that person shall be liable on
-- src:3577 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $1 million despite section 50(4).
@ref s 45S(1) (src:3573-3577)
GIVEN `the person commits an offence under section 50(2) or (3) as a provider of a regulated online communication service, with respect to documents or information relating to that service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45S(1) the person is liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1 million despite section 50(4)` MEANS
    IF `the person commits an offence under section 50(2) or (3) as a provider of a regulated online communication service, with respect to documents or information relating to that service` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3573 | 45S.—(1) Where the person that commits an offence under
-- src:3574 | section 50(2) or (3) is a provider of a regulated online
-- src:3575 | communication service and with respect to documents or
-- src:3576 | information relating to that service, that person shall be liable on
-- src:3577 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $1 million despite section 50(4).
@ref s 45S(1) (the ceiling) (src:3573-3577)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 45S(1) the most the provider can be fined` MEANS 1000000

-- src:3579 | (2) The power under section 50(1) to require the provision of
-- src:3580 | documents relating to an online communication service includes
-- src:3581 | power to require the production of documents held outside Singapore.
@ref s 45S(2) (src:3579-3581)
GIVEN `the documents relate to an online communication service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documents are held outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45S(2) the power under section 50(1) includes power to require their production` MEANS
    IF `the documents relate to an online communication service` THEN JUST `the documents are held outside Singapore` ELSE NOTHING

§ `45T. Interpretation of this Part`

-- src:3587 | “advocate”, in relation to any conduct, means counsel, promote,
-- src:3588 | encourage or urge the engaging in that conduct;
@ref s 45T(1) "advocate" (src:3587-3588)
GIVEN `it is to counsel, promote, encourage or urge the engaging in the conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45T(1) the person advocates the conduct` MEANS `it is to counsel, promote, encourage or urge the engaging in the conduct`

-- src:3589 | “child” means an individual who is below 18 years of age;
@ref s 45T(1) "child" (src:3589)
GIVEN `the age of the individual in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45T(1) the individual is a child` MEANS `the age of the individual in years` BELOW 18

-- src:3590 | “functionality”, in relation to an online communication service,
-- src:3591 | has the meaning given by section 2A;
@ref s 45T(1) "functionality" (src:3590-3591)
-- The meaning is in s 2A(5); the function is the same rule.
GIVEN `it is a functionality under section 2A(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45T(1) the feature is a functionality as section 2A gives the meaning` MEANS `it is a functionality under section 2A(5)`

-- src:3592 | “harm” includes harm to an individual’s mental health;
@ref s 45T(1) "harm" (src:3592)
GIVEN `it is harm to an individual's mental health` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45T(1) harm includes this` MEANS
    IF `it is harm to an individual's mental health` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3597 | “section 45H direction” means a direction given under
-- src:3598 | section 45H to a provider of an online communication
-- src:3599 | service, and includes such a direction that is varied under
-- src:3600 | section 59(3) on appeal;
@ref s 45T(1) "section 45H direction" (src:3597-3600)
GIVEN `it is a direction given under section 45H to a provider of an online communication service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is such a direction varied under section 59(3) on appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45T(1) the direction is a section 45H direction` MEANS
    `it is a direction given under section 45H to a provider of an online communication service` OR `it is such a direction varied under section 59(3) on appeal`

-- src:3602 | “section 45I blocking direction” means a direction given under
-- src:3603 | section 45I to a provider of an internet access service, and
-- src:3604 | includes such a direction varied under section 59(3) on
-- src:3605 | appeal;
@ref s 45T(1) "section 45I blocking direction" (src:3602-3605)
GIVEN `it is a direction given under section 45I to a provider of an internet access service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is such a direction varied under section 59(3) on appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45T(1) the direction is a section 45I blocking direction` MEANS
    `it is a direction given under section 45I to a provider of an internet access service` OR `it is such a direction varied under section 59(3) on appeal`

-- src:3607 | “social media service” means an electronic service that satisfies
-- src:3608 | all the following characteristics:
-- src:3610 | (a) the sole or primary purpose of the service is to enable
-- src:3611 | online interaction or linking between 2 or more end-
-- src:3612 | users (including enabling end-users to share content
-- src:3613 | for social purposes);
-- src:3615 | (b) the service allows end-users to communicate content
-- src:3616 | on the service;
-- src:3618 | (c) any other characteristics that are prescribed by Part
-- src:3619 | 10A regulations;
@ref s 45T(1) "social media service" (src:3607-3619)
GIVEN `it is an electronic service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its sole or primary purpose is to enable online interaction or linking between 2 or more end-users (including enabling end-users to share content for social purposes)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service allows end-users to communicate content on the service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has any other characteristic prescribed by Part 10A regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45T(1) the service is a social media service` MEANS
    `it is an electronic service` AND `its sole or primary purpose is to enable online interaction or linking between 2 or more end-users (including enabling end-users to share content for social purposes)` AND `the service allows end-users to communicate content on the service` AND `it has any other characteristic prescribed by Part 10A regulations`

-- src:3621 | “system or process” includes —
-- src:3623 | (a) a human or an automated system or process; and
-- src:3625 | (b) any technology;
@ref s 45T(1) "system or process" (src:3621-3625)
GIVEN `it is a human or an automated system or process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is any technology` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45T(1) system or process includes this` MEANS
    IF `it is a human or an automated system or process` OR `it is any technology` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3627 | “user-generated content” has the meaning given by section 2A.
@ref s 45T(1) "user-generated content" (src:3627)
-- The meaning is in s 2A(5); the function is the same rule.
GIVEN `it is user-generated content under section 2A(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45T(1) the content is user-generated content as section 2A gives the meaning` MEANS `it is user-generated content under section 2A(5)`

-- src:3629 | (2) To avoid doubt, “content” in this Part includes user-generated
-- src:3630 | content.
@ref s 45T(2) (src:3629-3630)
GIVEN `it is user-generated content` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45T(2) content in this Part includes this` MEANS
    IF `it is user-generated content` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3632 | (3) Where —
-- src:3634 | (a) by or under any provision of this Part or any Part 10A
-- src:3635 | regulations or any direction given under this Part, an act or
-- src:3636 | a thing is required or directed to be done within a particular
-- src:3637 | period or before a particular time, or any extended period
-- src:3638 | or time that the Authority may allow;
-- src:3640 | (b) failure to do that act or thing within the period or before the
-- src:3641 | time mentioned in paragraph (a) constitutes an offence;
-- src:3642 | and
-- src:3647 | (c) that act or thing is not done within the period or before the
-- src:3648 | time mentioned in paragraph (a),
-- src:3650 | the obligation to do that act or thing continues, even though that
-- src:3651 | period has expired or that time has passed, until that act or thing is
-- src:3652 | done.
@ref s 45T(3) (src:3632-3652)
GIVEN `a provision of this Part, Part 10A regulations or a direction requires an act or thing to be done within a particular period or before a particular time, or an extension the Authority allows` IS A BOOLEAN
      `failure to do it in that time constitutes an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was not done within that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45T(3) the obligation to do the act or thing continues after the period or time has passed, until it is done` MEANS
    IF `a provision of this Part, Part 10A regulations or a direction requires an act or thing to be done within a particular period or before a particular time, or an extension the Authority allows` AND `failure to do it in that time constitutes an offence` AND `it was not done within that time` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3654 | (4) For the purposes of this Part, an online communication service
-- src:3655 | has a Singapore end-user link if, and only if, all or any of the end-
-- src:3656 | users of that service are Singapore end-users.
@ref s 45T(4) (src:3654-3656)
GIVEN `all or any of the end-users of the service are Singapore end-users` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45T(4) the online communication service has a Singapore end-user link` MEANS
    `all or any of the end-users of the service are Singapore end-users`

§ `Context chapeau of section 45T(1)`

-- src:3586 | 45T.—(1) In this Part, unless the context otherwise requires —
@ref s 45T(1) chapeau (src:3586)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45T(1) the definitions apply in this Part` MEANS
    NOT `the context otherwise requires`
